      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T03:18:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like all of the affected boards are ones that we work on. The listed nucleo boards are development boards from ST that used the same MCU as our boards, so it looks like any changes only affect us. See [this table](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/docs/fingerprint/fingerprint.md#hardware).\n\nLooking at the blame history, it looks like [that config might have been added for the same reason](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/_/chromium/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5e93965e944370748a9d114e6de44c8bfe09047e) (vpalatin@ did most of the original FPMCU work).\n\nI haven\u0027t looked at this closely, but the name of the config implies that `%li` is a \"legacy format\". Is that the case? If it\u0027s not a legacy format, then combining them makes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "bf7063f1_63d13d9b",
      "revId": "ff4a3a5db35036159ee8d3d563aa7fe21e477a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
