      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T17:13:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Looks like all of the affected boards are ones that we work on. The listed nucleo boards are development boards from ST that used the same MCU as our boards, so it looks like any changes only affect us. See  this table .\n\nOh, I didn\u0027t realize the Nucleo boards were the MCU dev boards. That definitely reduces the risk of changes here.\n\n\u003e I haven\u0027t looked at this closely, but the name of the config implies that  %li  is a \"legacy format\". Is that the case? If it\u0027s not a legacy format, then combining them makes sense.\n\nThe name \"legacy format\" is a bit misleading because prior to disabling `%li` it was explicitly assumed 64-bit ints. I suspect the intent was actually \"standard printf format\" rather than \"legacy printf format\" but it\u0027s hard to say for sure.\n\nI was initially hesitant to mess with this format but based on what we\u0027ve seen in here I think we can merge them without issue.",
      "parentUuid": "caeeb378_4ebfe79c",
      "revId": "ff4a3a5db35036159ee8d3d563aa7fe21e477a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
